## 7) **Destructor**  
Automatically called when object goes out of scope; use to release resources.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class Demo {
public:
    Demo() { cout << "Constructor: resource acquired\n"; }
    ~Demo() { cout << "Destructor: resource released\n"; }
};

void f() {
    Demo d;   // constructor runs here
    cout << "Inside f()\n";
} // d goes out of scope here -> destructor runs

int main() {
    cout << "Before calling f()\n";
    f();
    cout << "After calling f()\n";
    return 0;
}
```

